From 827887f772dee20c525317845c9608fe9a42e473 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexMitchellMus <12004932+AlexMitchellMus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:44:14 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: lower memory.grow and memory.size intrinsics

core::arch::wasm32::{memory_grow,memory_size} resolve to
InstanceKind::LlvmIntrinsic with the LLVM names llvm.wasm.memory.grow.i32
and llvm.wasm.memory.size.i32. The generic LLVM intrinsic fallback
replaced them with a trap, so a growable allocator could not work.

Lower them to calls to clif-to-wasm's reserved helper names, which
clif-to-wasm turns into the wasm memory.grow and memory.size instructions.
Both LLVM intrinsics take the memory index as a first argument; stdarch
statically requires it to be zero, so only the value operand is
forwarded. Add a compile-only wasm regression example, enabled in
config.txt so a wasm-target run of the test suite executes it.

This depends on clif-to-wasm's WasmIntrinsic helpers and on cg_clif's
wasm backend, which is not upstream yet; the patch applies cleanly to
upstream but is only reachable once that backend lands.

License: MIT OR Apache-2.0, as a contribution to the Rust project.
